WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.667
(dramatic orchestral music)

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.193
- [Ana] Jude is the light of my life.

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.593
He's on the autism spectrum,

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:16.225
and so that makes him extra special.

00:00:16.225 --> 00:00:17.543
(video game controller clicking)

00:00:17.543 --> 00:00:19.033
- [Jude] Justin, Justin.

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:20.440
- [Ana] I don't want him to be stuck

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.747
in just a video game world.

00:00:22.747 --> 00:00:26.073
(tires crunching)

00:00:26.073 --> 00:00:28.573
(car beeping)

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:33.430
Hiking can bring you strength,

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:37.543
and I want to impart some of that to him.

00:00:41.743 --> 00:00:44.326
(wind whooshing)

00:00:47.154 --> 00:00:49.610
(footsteps crunching)

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:51.890
My parents, they tried to raise me

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:54.640
to be a traditional Latina.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.440
When they thought of outdoor activities,

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:00.783
it was meant for boys, so I was told no.

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:04.253
(gentle music)

00:01:05.992 --> 00:01:07.088
It didn't always work.

00:01:07.088 --> 00:01:10.163
I seemed to always find
a way to break the rules.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.360
2012 was a pivotal year for me.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:25.040
My mother was diagnosed
with stage four lung cancer.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.910
While she was in hospice, my son's father

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:31.273
decided that he wanted to end
our six-year relationship,

00:01:33.066 --> 00:01:35.408
and then my mother died two days later.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.884
My son was 4 1/2.

00:01:39.884 --> 00:01:42.801
(dramatic music)

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:47.525
It all just shattered me.

00:01:47.525 --> 00:01:49.723
(person breathing heavily)

00:01:49.723 --> 00:01:52.023
I was in a really dark place.

00:01:56.690 --> 00:02:00.653
I literally, one day I
had this urge to get out.

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:05.170
Getting to the top of the
mountain is a journey.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:08.660
I've learned so much about myself

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:11.623
and what I'm capable of
by taking that journey.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:16.985
I want Jude to feel a sense
of accomplishment himself

00:02:16.985 --> 00:02:18.976
when we finish a hike.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:24.720
Jude does not particularly love hiking.

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.370
I have tried to get him outdoors.

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:29.550
I push him.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.853
I want him to expand his horizon.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:37.290
I do worry about his future.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.100
I want him to be happy.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.075
I want him to find love.

00:02:41.075 --> 00:02:43.110
(gentle piano music)

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:44.670
Come here.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:45.727
Try that one.

00:02:45.727 --> 00:02:46.560
Is that good?

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:47.393
- Yeah.

00:02:47.393 --> 00:02:48.226
- All right, cool.

00:02:48.226 --> 00:02:49.870
You want to lead the way?

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:50.703
- [Jude] I guess.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:51.536
- [Ana] All right.

00:02:51.536 --> 00:02:52.369
- [Jude] You're too slow.

00:02:52.369 --> 00:02:53.712
- [Ana] I'm too slow?

00:02:53.712 --> 00:02:55.110
What?

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:55.960
Seriously?

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:57.690
They look pretty, don't they?

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:00.650
All these things that
I've struggled through,

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:03.040
when it comes to the end of the day,

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:07.470
what keeps me sane is
knowing that Jude is okay,

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.100
'cause he is the light of my life,

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:13.540
and hearing his voice, seeing
him, cuddling with him,

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:17.450
it makes just about everything go away.

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:19.648
- [Jude] There's a bunch of flowers.

00:03:19.648 --> 00:03:21.055
- [Ana] Yeah, what do you think those are?

00:03:21.055 --> 00:03:21.963
Do you know the name?

00:03:21.963 --> 00:03:23.568
- [Jude] No, lupins.

00:03:23.568 --> 00:03:24.888
- [Ana] They're lupins?

00:03:24.888 --> 00:03:26.338
How did you know that?

00:03:26.338 --> 00:03:28.024
- [Jude] 'Cause you told me.

00:03:28.024 --> 00:03:30.135
- [Ana] Oh. (laughs)

00:03:30.135 --> 00:03:32.126
(gentle music)

00:03:32.126 --> 00:03:34.623
- [Jude] Look at the wildflowers here.

00:03:34.623 --> 00:03:35.873
- [Ana] Yeah.

